{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1114 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8d31a185727ccd73330617911af3fa40b0e37c35947ca60e8ded2b8b9f31d990" :edb/db-before-t 1113 :edb/db-after-t 1114 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534426 50 #inst "2026-10-07T02:44:27.106Z" 13194139534426 true] [17592186092133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287647 13194139534426 true] [17592186092133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287654 13194139534426 true] [17592186092133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287661 13194139534426 true] [17592186092134 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287668 13194139534426 true] [17592186092765 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534426 true] [17592186092765 1100 "Consider a matrix equation $A^{-1}x = B^{-1}d$, where $A$ and $B$ are $5 \\cdot 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5 \\cdot 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x$." 13194139534426 false] [17592186092765 1100 "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186092765 1145 "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287647 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287648 13194139534426 true] [17592186287647 1089 "q-10074" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287647 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534426 true] [17592186287647 1100 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z=-1-x \\\\ 4y=-5z \\\\ x+6z-3=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287647 1113 #uuid "e436b484-45cd-5959-9069-2880512ec233" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287647 1145 "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4y+5z=0 \\\\ x+6z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(24)-2(-5)+3(0-4) \\\\  & =24+10-12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 5 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{11} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{11} \\\\ \\frac{8}{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}.$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287649 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287650 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287651 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287652 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287653 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1041 "selection" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287651 13194139534426 true] [17592186287648 1110 #uuid "ed131fa2-13cf-592a-be0c-f93fee5f0963" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287649 1034 "x=\\frac{15}{11},y=\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287649 1111 #uuid "3913b813-19e1-5838-a7ce-25c5f75b98b1" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287650 1034 "x=-15,y=-10,z=8" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287650 1111 #uuid "7f7fbde2-1a21-5fb1-8d83-65e0637b0829" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287651 1034 "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287651 1111 #uuid "d49ea752-b50e-5647-ba94-f4bf5951285c" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287652 1034 "x=-30,y=-20,z=16" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287652 1111 #uuid "42da5cbf-1dcc-5f8e-aff0-1ee1c79574da" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287653 1034 "x=15,y=10,z=8" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287653 1111 #uuid "5fdb890a-69a1-5c8a-b553-5afded12115b" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287654 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287655 13194139534426 true] [17592186287654 1089 "q-104536" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287654 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534426 true] [17592186287654 1100 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2z=2+2y \\\\ 2y+4z=2x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287654 1113 #uuid "528b601b-5416-5158-83e1-ea8ffb44a5a4" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287654 1145 "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z=2 \\\\ -2x+2y+4z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-4)+(4-4) \\\\  & =-4+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=2+1+0=3.$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287656 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287657 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287658 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287659 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287660 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1041 "selection" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287656 13194139534426 true] [17592186287655 1110 #uuid "6e58b42b-ea48-5337-bb06-7cf540036ffb" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287656 1034 "3" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287656 1111 #uuid "40398599-c736-5231-83f6-dd91cf084a44" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287657 1034 "2" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287657 1111 #uuid "040386b6-5143-5e39-a9e4-c69c7af3cada" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287658 1034 "1" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287658 1111 #uuid "f5b433aa-17d2-5e91-a08f-3477affa21f3" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287659 1034 "4" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287659 1111 #uuid "b996bbe6-77e2-52b4-a15a-6bcb715fd96d" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287660 1034 "0" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534426 true] [17592186287660 1111 #uuid "9330039e-54ee-52a6-9da7-c7c1b7494f8e" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287661 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287662 13194139534426 true] [17592186287661 1089 "q-104541" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287661 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534426 true] [17592186287661 1100 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+z+x=2 \\\\ -3z+y=3 \\\\ 2x+y=4-4z\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287661 1113 #uuid "cf9ff59f-8ec8-569a-88c2-1ac3dd73e105" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287661 1145 "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=2 \\\\ y-3z=3 \\\\ 2x+y+4z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4+3)-(0+6)+(0-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=11,y=-6,z=-3.$" 13194139534426 true] [17592186287662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287663 13194139534426 true] [17592186287662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287664 13194139534426 true] [17592186287662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287665 13194139534426 true] [17592186287662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287666 13194139534426 true] [17592186287662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287667 13194139534426 true] [17592186287662 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534426 true] [17592